3. Solving for Optimal Mounting Parameters
Step A: Height Selection (h)
If h is too low (<10 cm), the camera looks straight into the side of the pillar. At 15 cm range, a 10 cm pillar overflows the camera frame vertically.

If h is too high (>22 cm), the center of gravity shifts upward, increasing chassis body roll during 1.5 m/s Ackermann steering turns.

Optimal Height (h): 14 cm to 16 cm from the track surface (measured to the center of the camera lens).

